<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<PLUGIN name="silo-streams" author="Bryan Mannos" version="2026.11.15c" min="7.0.0" launch="Settings/SiloStreams" icon="icon.png" pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/b-mannos/unraid-silo-streams/main/silo-streams.plg" support="https://github.com/b-mannos/unraid-silo-streams/issues">
  <CHANGES># Changelog

## 2026.11.15c

First public release, prepared for Community Applications review.

- Ships the plugin with its original icon and public release metadata for
  Community Applications listing.
- Includes earlier fixes: the plugin's own CSRF validation now works alongside
  Unraid's standard `csrf_token` handling on the settings page.
- Includes earlier fixes: signed relative Silo artwork URLs load through the
  same-origin Unraid poster endpoint, so posters render without direct browser
  access to the internal Silo address.
- Adds a stable public installer URL for Unraid's update checker.
</CHANGES>
  <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
    <INLINE>
set -eu
command -v php &gt;/dev/null || { echo 'Silo Streams requires PHP 8.2 and cURL.'; exit 1; }
php -r 'exit(PHP_VERSION_ID &gt;= 80200 &amp;&amp; extension_loaded("curl") ? 0 : 1);' || { echo 'Silo Streams requires PHP 8.2 and cURL.'; exit 1; }
umask 077
mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/silo-streams
# FAT mount options govern flash permissions; chmod is best effort.
chmod 700 /boot/config/plugins/silo-streams 2&gt;/dev/null || true
</INLINE>
  </FILE>
